: []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The versioned history of one entry, read and written in one place that every SQLite library store calls (001 §C 'Versions are immutable', 'Hybrid shape'; .spec-md §5 `LibraryDbContext`). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 62-64), after step 64's members, a type extension on `LibraryDbContext` whose members each carry step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark. They run inside `LibraryDatabase.run` (step 62), which catches every exception. They stage changes on the context and never save, so a store ends its `run` with one `SaveChanges ()` and an operation's writes land together or not at all. (1) Reads, every row read through `toStoredVersion` (step 63), whose failure is answered: `tryLatestStored (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>`, the version the entry's `LatestVersion` row names, `None` without that row; `tryStoredVersion (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>`, whatever its lifecycle; `storedVersionsOf (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<StoredEntryVersion list, StorageError>`, ascending by version; and `latestStoredOfKind (kind : LibraryEntryKind) : Result<StoredEntryVersion list, StorageError>`, the latest version of every entry of the kind, in no promised order. (2) Writes: `stageVersion (stored : StoredEntryVersion) : Result<unit, StorageError>` adds the version's row (`versionRow`, step 63), or overwrites every column of the tracked row holding its id and version, and makes the version's facet and sample-material rows exactly its envelope's `facetRows` and `sampleMaterialRows` (step 64); `stageLatest (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : unit` makes the entry's `LatestVersion` row name the version, adding the row when absent; and `stageRemoval (id : LibraryEntryId) : unit` removes the entry's latest row and every version row, whose facet, sample-material and pulled-source rows the cascade removes (step 60). (3) The version rule's outcomes, so no store re-implements them: `stageNewEntry (content : LibraryEntryContent) : Result<unit, StorageError>` seals the content (`sealed`, step 30) and stages it as its entry's version and latest under `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`; `stageEdit (latest : StoredEntryVersion) (decision : VersionDecision) (content : LibraryEntryContent) : Result<unit, StorageError>` takes the edited value's content at the latest's version and stages nothing for `KeepCurrent`, the sealed content under the latest's state for `MutateInPlace`, and for `MintNextVersion` the sealed `{ content with version = latest.envelope.content.version.next }` under `{ ActiveEntry; VersionUnpinned }`, made the latest. No cache, retry, query option or other member is added. (4) The fixture. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains `freshLibraryDatabase () : LibraryDatabase`: a new `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString "Data Source=:memory:")` holding every envelope of `catalogueData ()` as its version 1 and latest under `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`, staged through `stageVersion` and `stageLatest` in one `run`. An error fails the calling fact with its `describe`; the caller disposes the database. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. (5) Facts, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, each disposing what it opens. (a) `the fixture library database holds every Built-in entry as its version 1 and latest`: for each kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all`, `latestStoredOfKind` answers exactly the ids of the catalogue's envelopes of that kind, each version 1, equal to its envelope, active and unpinned; and `tryLatestStored` of a test-local GUID answers `None`. (b) `staging a version overwrites its row and its relational rows, and the latest names the staged version`: `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s version 1, restaged pinned with the `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId` structure (its content resealed), answers pinned through `tryStoredVersion` and has exactly the langasite and silicon sample-material rows at version 1; a renamed version 2 of `MaterialIds.silicon`, staged with `stageLatest`, is what `tryLatestStored` answers, while `tryStoredVersion` of version 1 still answers the catalogue's envelope and `storedVersionsOf` answers versions 1 and 2 in order. (c) `stageEdit keeps, mutates or mints exactly as its decision says`: over Silicon's latest, `KeepCurrent` changes no row; `MutateInPlace` of a renamed Silicon rewrites version 1 under its state and its `BuiltInProvenance`; `MintNextVersion` of a further renamed Silicon adds version 2, active and unpinned, as the latest; and `stageNewEntry` of a test-local material's content makes its version 1 the latest. (d) `staging a removal deletes every version of the entry and its relational rows`: after (b)'s version 2, `stageRemoval` of Silicon leaves no version, latest or facet row of it, while every other entry keeps its latest row.

**Acceptance.** After the operations land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture library database holds every Built-in entry as its version 1 and latest`, `staging a version overwrites its row and its relational rows, and the latest names the staged version`, `stageEdit keeps, mutates or mints exactly as its decision says` and `staging a removal deletes every version of the entry and its relational rows`; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.
